T1  - Multiple pituitary hormone deficiency (MPHD) associated with normal height, absent puberty and obesity.
A1  - Doknic, Mirjana
A1  - Pekic, Sandra
A1  - Djurovic, Marina
A1  - Zivkovic, Vladimir
A1  - Popovic, Vera
Y1  - 2004//
N2  - We present a 22-year old girl with MPHD and a normal pituitary imaging (MRI) who grew to normal size without GH. She was very obese. At age 19 years replacement therapy with hydrocortisone, L-thyroxine and sex steroids was started. Despite severe growth hormone deficiency according to the provocative tests and decreased IGF I level our patient grew normally. On follow up at age 22 she is 174cm tall.
